The Requirement Analysis Phase identifies what the ComicCraft-AI system needs to provide, what technologies are required, and how users will interact with the application.

1. Functional Requirements

The system should provide the following functions:

User Input – Users can enter a basic comic idea or story prompt.
Genre Selection – Users can select genres such as fantasy, comedy, adventure, mystery and science fiction.
Story Generation – Gemini generates a complete story based on the user's idea.
Character Generation – The system generates character names, roles, personalities and descriptions.
Scene Generation – The story is divided into suitable scenes or comic panels.
Dialogue Generation – Gemini generates dialogues for the characters.
Story Modification – Users can edit or regenerate the generated content.
Comic Structure – The system organizes the story into panels, scenes and dialogues.
Preview – Users can preview the generated comic story.
Save/Export – Users can save or export their completed comic story.
2. Non-Functional Requirements

The system should satisfy the following requirements:

Usability: The interface should be simple and easy to understand.
Performance: Story generation should be reasonably fast.
Reliability: The system should handle invalid or incomplete prompts properly.
Security: User data and API credentials should be protected.
Scalability: The system should be capable of supporting more users and features later.
Maintainability: The application should be easy to update and maintain.
Responsiveness: The interface should work properly on different screen sizes.
3. Hardware Requirements
Computer or laptop
Minimum 4 GB RAM
Internet connection
Keyboard and mouse
Sufficient storage for application files and generated content
4. Software Requirements
Requirement	Technology
Operating System	Windows / Linux / macOS
Frontend	HTML, CSS, JavaScript / React
Backend	Python / Flask or Node.js
AI Model	Google Gemini API
Database	Firebase / MySQL
Browser	Chrome / Edge / Firefox
Development Tool	VS Code
5. AI Requirements

The system requires access to a Gemini model through the Google Gemini API. Gemini is used for:

Story generation
Character development
Scene descriptions
Dialogue generation
Story continuation
Content modification
6. User Requirements

The user should be able to:

Enter Idea
     ↓
Select Genre
     ↓
Generate Story
     ↓
Create Characters
     ↓
Generate Scenes & Dialogues
     ↓
Edit Content
     ↓
Preview Comic
     ↓
Save / Export
7. Requirement Summary

The requirement analysis establishes that ComicCraft-AI needs a user-friendly interface, Gemini-powered story generation, character and dialogue creation, scene/panel organization, editing facilities and an option to save or export the final comic. These requirements provide the foundation for designing and developing the complete system.
